# 2026-10-14: ImageMagick `import` debris. Running a Python file under bash
# (`bash tests/foo.py`) makes its `import os` / `import re` lines execute
# /usr/bin/import, which writes a 6.4M PostScript file named after the "image
# filename" into the cwd. Observed once in this repo root (six files: os, re,
# subprocess, sys, tempfile, unittest) and once in automation/. Both are silent:
# the caller still exits 0. Ignore the pattern rather than chase every caller.
/os
/re
/sys
/tempfile
/unittest
/subprocess
/*.ps
